  "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 36-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate. Stack topology: Air incident medium | Ta2O5(1) | SiO2(2) | Ta2O5(3) | SiO2(4) | Ta2O5(5) | SiO2(6) | Ta2O5(7) | SiO2(8) | Ta2O5(9) | SiO2(10) | Ta2O5(11) | SiO2(12) | Ta2O5(13) | SiO2(14) | Ta2O5(15) | SiO2(16) | Ta2O5(17) | SiO2(18) | Ta2O5(19) | SiO2(20) | Ta2O5(21) | SiO2(22) | Ta2O5(23) | SiO2(24) | Ta2O5(25) | SiO2(26) | Ta2O5(27) | SiO2(28) | Ta2O5(29) | SiO2(30) | Ta2O5(31) | SiO2(32) | Ta2O5(33) | SiO2(34) | Ta2O5(35) | SiO2(36) | Fused Silica substrate. All 36 layers have individual thickness optimization variables bounded 30-340 nm. Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness: Ta2O5 layers at 560 nm/(4*n_Ta2O5), SiO2 layers at 560 nm/(4*n_SiO2). Illumination: 0 degree incidence, unpolarized light. Simulation wavelength grid must cover 350-1100 nm with sufficient resolution to evaluate target bands: 355 nm (single wavelength), 355-365 nm (band), 420-700 nm (passband), 1030-1080 nm (band). Optimize using gradient-based method to maximize passband transmittance while minimizing stopband transmittance. Report thicknesses_nm for all 36 layers, best_target_score, valid_candidates count, and tightest_margin. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize thicknesses of a 36-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 stack on fused silica to maximize transmission in 420–700 nm while minimizing transmission at 355 nm, 355–365 nm, and 1030–1080 nm under normal incidence with unpolarized light across 350–1100 nm.",
